 "about_text": "galerie a is a Tokyo project founded in 2020 by Nobuhiko Akiyoshi, a former buyer and wholesale agent who had worked for over a decade with domestic and international fashion designers before launching this gallery. Conceived during the COVID-19 pandemic, it operates as an online gallery that also stages physical, short-run exhibitions in Akiyoshi's own space, allowing visitors to experience works in person during limited open-gallery days. The program focuses on introducing Japan-based makers working by hand, spanning leather craft, textile sculpture, woodwork, and photography-informed leather goods, with an emphasis on artisans who pursue original, material-driven expression.",
